---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Providers">
  <p>
    The API supports several lyrics providers. They differ in coverage, timing detail and response format.
    The default endpoint uses TTML, and you can pick another provider when you need to.
  </p>

  <h2>Available providers</h2>

  <div class="provider-cards">
    <div class="provider-card">
      <div class="provider-header">
        <h3>TTML</h3>
        <span class="badge default">Default</span>
      </div>
      <p>Syllable-synced lyrics with precise timing.</p>
      <table class="provider-details">
        <tr>
          <td>Endpoint</td>
          <td><code>/getLyrics</code> or <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sync level</td>
          <td>Syllable</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Best for</td>
          <td>Karaoke-style display, syllable highlighting</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Response format</td>
          <td>TTML XML</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="provider-card">
      <div class="provider-header">
        <h3>Kugou</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Line-synced lyrics with broad coverage.</p>
      <table class="provider-details">
        <tr>
          <td>Endpoint</td>
          <td><code>/kugou/getLyrics</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sync level</td>
          <td>Line</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Best for</td>
          <td>Line-by-line display, fallback coverage</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Response format</td>
          <td>LRC-style text</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="provider-card">
      <div class="provider-header">
        <h3>QQ</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Word-timed lyrics, useful when TTML has no match.</p>
      <table class="provider-details">
        <tr>
          <td>Endpoint</td>
          <td><code>/qq/getLyrics</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sync level</td>
          <td>Word</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Best for</td>
          <td>Word highlighting when TTML returns no results</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Response format</td>
          <td><a href="/docs/qrc-format">QRC XML</a></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Choosing a provider</h2>
  <p>Use the default TTML provider unless you need something else:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>TTML has the best overall coverage and precision. Use it for karaoke-style syllable highlighting.</li>
    <li>Kugou is line-synced with broad coverage. Use it if TTML returns no results.</li>
    <li>QQ is word-timed. Use it if TTML returns no results and you still want timing finer than a line.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Response differences</h2>
  <p>
    Each provider returns a different format. <a href="/braccato/parsers"><code>@braccato/parsers</code></a>
    reads all three into the same line structure, so you can switch providers without changing your
    rendering code.
  </p>

  <h3>TTML response</h3>
  <p><code>/getLyrics</code> returns:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "ttml": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\"?>..."
}`}</code></pre>
  <p><code>/ttml/getLyrics</code> uses the same shape as the other provider-specific endpoints:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "lyrics": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\"?>...",
  "provider": "ttml"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Kugou response</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "lyrics": "[00:12.34]First line of lyrics\\n[00:15.67]Second line...",
  "provider": "kugou"
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>QQ response</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "lyrics": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?><QrcInfos>...[5767,324]Wanderlust - (5767,109)The (5876,106)Weeknd(5982,109)...</QrcInfos>",
  "provider": "qq"
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The QRC body sits inside an XML envelope, with word timing after each word. See
    <a href="/docs/qrc-format">QRC format</a> for the structure and how to parse it.
  </p>

  <h2>Provider-specific headers</h2>
  <p>
    The provider-specific endpoints send an <code>X-Provider</code> header that indicates which provider served
    the response. <code>/getLyrics</code> does not send it:
  </p>
  <pre><code>X-Provider: ttml</code></pre>

  <h2>Cache isolation</h2>
  <p>
    Each provider has its own cache namespace. A song cached via TTML will not be served
    when you request via Kugou or QQ, and the other way around. That way you always get the format you asked for.
  </p>
  <p>Cache key prefixes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>ttml_lyrics:</code> for TTML</li>
    <li><code>kugou_lyrics:</code> for Kugou</li>
    <li><code>qq_lyrics:</code> for QQ</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <code>/getLyrics</code> and <code>/ttml/getLyrics</code> both use <code>ttml_lyrics:</code>, but format the album and
    duration in the key differently, so they share entries only when neither album nor duration is sent.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .provider-cards {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .provider-card {
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-5);
  }

  .provider-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .provider-header h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .badge {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .badge.default {
    background-color: rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.1);
    color: var(--success);
  }

  .provider-card > p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .provider-details {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  .provider-details td {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .provider-details td:first-child {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    width: 120px;
  }

  .provider-details tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
</style>
